### Scapia Price Watch — API scratchpad
# JetBrains HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client. Run requests top-to-bottom for a full demo.
# Start the server first:  .venv/bin/python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@userId = demo-user
@productId = gully-baaz-faris-black
@dtcSource = {{productId}}:DTC

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Catalogue
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### List products (derived Scapia + DTC prices)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### Get one product
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### Price history for a product (SCAPIA + DTC observations)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/observations

### Crawl runs for a product (crawler-result UI feed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/crawl-runs

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Watches
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Create a watch  (run this first; later requests read its response for the id)
# @name createWatch
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/watches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "productId": "{{productId}}"
}

### List this user's watches
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/watches?userId={{userId}}

### Get one watch (uses the id from createWatch's response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/watches/{{createWatch.response.body.$.id}}

### Register a "Buy on Scapia" click (conversion metric)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/watches/{{createWatch.response.body.$.id}}/buy-click

### Cancel a watch
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/watches/{{createWatch.response.body.$.id}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Demo controls
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Set Scapia price (updates product.scapia_price + logs an INTERNAL observation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/demo/products/{{productId}}/scapia-price
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 3790
}

### Set DTC price (writes a mock crawl_run — same path the AI crawler uses)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/demo/dtc-sources/{{dtcSource}}/dtc-price
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 3790
}

### Force-evaluate all active watches now (instant on-stage trigger)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/demo/evaluate-now

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Funnel stats
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/stats

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Crawler API (the AI web crawler's integration surface)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Worklist — DTC sources with an ACTIVE watch (create a watch first to see entries)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/internal/crawl-worklist

### Ingest a crawl result (status ∈ OK|DEGRADED|FAILED; price null iff FAILED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/internal/crawl-runs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dtcSourceId": "{{dtcSource}}",
  "status": "OK",
  "price": 3690,
  "productName": "Gully Number 001 – Baaz Faris Black",
  "confidence": 0.95
}

### Ingest a FAILED crawl (no price; backend keeps last known DTC price)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/internal/crawl-runs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dtcSourceId": "{{dtcSource}}",
  "status": "FAILED",
  "error": "price selector not found"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WebSocket (not runnable from an .http file):
#   ws://localhost:8000/ws/notifications?userId=demo-user
# Server pushes { "type":"PRICE_MATCH", ... } when a watch triggers.
# Try it from a browser console or:  websocat "ws://localhost:8000/ws/notifications?userId=demo-user"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
